er sister  on a second validation so thank you for  inviting me to speak today  Thank You Jeffrey and Leah for your  informative presentations we will now  start the Q&amp;A portion of the webinar if  you have a question you'd like to ask  please do so now just click on the ask a  question box located on the far left of  your screen  we'll answer as many of your questions  as we have time for before we start we  have a poll question we popping up on  your screen now we appreciate your  participation  you  okay let's get started our first  question is I'm new to NGS does your AP  consulting service provide data analysis  or bioinformatics consulting  you  so it does we do part of the AV packages  that we will assist you in your data  analysis during the course of your  analytical validation there will be a  couple files that we request as Lea  mentioned in our presentation we do set  up a thermal Fisher cloud site where the  data can be uploaded to the files  relatively pretty large depending on the  number of sample they're condensed down  into a single dip file but we'll walk  through you at the beginning on how you  pull those files that we'll need and  then from there we're able to access the  view VCF files and assist you through  your data analysis for that we also  there's another file that we request  from a torn suite where we do  comprehensive data analysis on how the  coverage analysis route for your DNA  portion the assay is working  great thank you okay next question can  you expand upon the benefits that your  customers have experienced during the AV  consulting process  so maybe I'll wait for that one and then  Lee I don't know if you you know want to  fill in with the second answer with that  you know I mean we've been talking with  customers and we've been working with  customers you know a lot of it is the  product management we literally put  together a schedule that will tell you  you know on you know what chip what day  what is serving what barcode to run each  sample you know just to really take the  burden of knowing what to do for your ad  you know off the labs hands also you  know with one reading the solid tumor  assays as we mentioned and providing  samples and controls we do have access  to a biorepository where we're able to  provide FFP tumor resection sections as  well as different you know contrives and  cell line controls that you'll need for  your ad and the data analysis assistance  as well  and you know I mentioned in my  presentation that we are going through  upwards of 20 runs again depending on  multiplexing the upwards of 20 runs  during a short timeframe so having  someone that's you know very comfortable  in doing this data analysis and you know  specifically on ER instrumentation is  even beneficial because we're able to  you know easily you know get this data  you can get through analyzing this data  and get it compiled and then you know  review it with each lab so while they're  learning the process well they're you  know when I li can probably speak to  this better but while they weren't still  trying to learn the process of running  the assay and get comfortable with the  everyday every day operational flow of  their next gen so you can see now say  where you in the background you know are  compiling data for them  yeah yeah if you have anything that  yes as you were saying Jeff you know it  was certainly beneficial to have a  presence in the background of you know  somebody who knows what they're doing it  you know any validation is difficult the  very first time you're really wandering  into foreign territory and you're not  quite sure if you're doing a ride and  they're trying to meet all the  regulatory so it was great to have you  know dedicated team to answer questions  for us you know to get the workflow to  get the process to get the daily feel as  to what was supposed to do what we're  supposed to do and you know  understanding the instruments better I  again the checklist were beneficial  because there are so many components to  this that happens simultaneously you  know the a/v the regulatory you know the  document writing you know having a  template provided for an SOP is great  you know because we can take what we  need from that and then fit it into our  own process  you know because each lab is  individualized on how they handle you  know procedures and policies so we were  able to have some guidance and to fit  that into our needs so yeah it was it  was really great to have a leader and  guidance you know to to get us through  this this first one and as I already  said that the second one and then after  that you know we'll be on our own  great thank you looks like we have time  for one more question what's the best  way for my company to ensure that we  have what we need to complete the ad  process  you know I would say get to know your  guidelines get a hold of the Jenny's the  Jenny's paper you know read through the  cap molecular checklist read through the  cfli guidelines and you know know what  each of these different regulatory  agencies required for expression for  analytical validation you know to do  that that is the most important thing  that you know you could do and then you  know as we mentioned in the slide where  I went over questions ask yourself those  questions and really make sure that in  addition you know to asking yourself  those questions that you have your you  know your analytical validation planned  out I mean plan in the planning is the  most important part in you know in early  days of us doing the analytical  validations and you know casseroles you  know it's if you go by the fly by the  seat of your pants method that's  typically where you'll see a validation  dry dry out you know into a year because  you're you know you're you're not  planned and you're just picking samples  out of okay maybe I'll run these snacks  maybe run these and so you don't be very  prepared for a validation and then you